/// known-gap: interp yall_parse values never compare equal to map literals
/// yall_write output reads back as the same value for multiline strings anywhere (block, inline, edge newlines, a `"""` line) and for strings with `:` or a leading `#` in small maps
cases | [{"a": "x\ny\n"}, {"a": "\nx"}, {"a": ["p\nq"]}, {"a": {"b": "p\nq"}}, {"a": "p\nq"}, {"t": "before\n\"\"\"\nafter"}, {"o": {"w": "a:b"}}, {"o": {"h": "#x", "u": 1}}]
repeat cases as c
  say(:yall_parse(:yall_write(c), "t.yall") == c)
xx
